    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="concept_marmot_1_1_math_1_1_differentiation_1_1_automatic_1_1_vector_mode_1_1_expression" kindref="compound">Expression</ref> node of a binary operation f( a, b ) with two non-constant operands. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>A</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>stored type of the first operand (see <ref refid="_marmot_automatic_differentiation_vector_mode_8h_1a23ecfd9081c6547128d6f35e4787a7f2" kindref="member">Operand</ref>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>B</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>stored type of the second operand (see <ref refid="_marmot_automatic_differentiation_vector_mode_8h_1a23ecfd9081c6547128d6f35e4787a7f2" kindref="member">Operand</ref>)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The derivatives are partialA * a.dx( i ) + partialB * b.dx( i ), with the partial derivatives evaluated once at construction. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
